5. **Zoom and reflow**
 Zoom browser to 200% — does content reflow without horizontal scrolling or clipping?
 Test at 400% zoom for WCAG 2.1 AA's "reflow" criterion if targeting that level.
6. **Forms and error handling**
 Every input has a visible, programmatically-linked label
 Errors are described in text (not just color), announced to screen readers, and tied to the specific field
7. **Touch targets (mobile)**
Interactive elements at least 44×44 CSS pixels, with enough spacing to avoid mis-taps
Suggested order of operations

Automated scan → keyboard pass → contrast check → screen reader spot-check → zoom/reflow test → fix critical/blocking issues first, then major, then polish.

If you want, I can run a structured audit against a specific page or Figma file — I have an accessibility-review workflow that outputs a prioritized findings table (issue, WCAG criterion, severity, fix). Just share a URL, screenshot, or describe the screen. 


